## Background and Motivation

Almost all numeric types have `Parse` and `TryParse` ReadOnlySpan<char> overload, I think it's good for `nint` to have them too.
Edit: `int` also has `TryFormat` method which contains `ReadOnlySpan<char>` parameter, so I added `TryFormat`.

<!--
We welcome API proposals! We have a process to evaluate the value and shape of new API. There is an overview of our process [here](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/master/docs/project/api-review-process.md). This template will help us gather the information we need to start the review process.
First, please describe the purpose and value of the new API here.
-->

## Proposed API

```diff
namespace System
{
    public class IntPtr {
+        public static IntPtr Parse(ReadOnlySpan<char> s, NumberStyles style = NumberStyles.Integer, IFormatProvider? provider = null) { }
+        public static bool TryParse(ReadOnlySpan<char> s, NumberStyles style, IFormatProvider? provider, out IntPtr result) { }
+        public static bool TryParse(ReadOnlySpan<char> s, out IntPtr result) { }
+        public bool TryFormat(Span<char> destination, out int charsWritten, ReadOnlySpan<char> format = default, IFormatProvider? provider = null) { }
     }
}
```

```diff
namespace System
{
    public class UIntPtr {
+        public static UIntPtr Parse(ReadOnlySpan<char> s, NumberStyles style = NumberStyles.Integer, IFormatProvider? provider = null) { }
+        public static bool TryParse(ReadOnlySpan<char> s, NumberStyles style, IFormatProvider? provider, out UIntPtr result) { }
+        public static bool TryParse(ReadOnlySpan<char> s, out UIntPtr result) { }
+        public bool TryFormat(Span<char> destination, out int charsWritten, ReadOnlySpan<char> format = default, IFormatProvider? provider = null) { }
     }
}
```
Update 2021.1.6: Change `Parse` and `TryParse` to match Int32 and Int64's signature and add `TryFormat`.
Update 2021.1.12: Add nuint
